diff --git a/ros2_ws/src/cleany_navigation/README.md b/ros2_ws/src/cleany_navigation/README.md
index 446b7cf..6f1a0df 100644
--- a/ros2_ws/src/cleany_navigation/README.md
+++ b/ros2_ws/src/cleany_navigation/README.md
@@ -698,3 +698,30 @@ pose, velocity, footprint and one sufficient obstacle cell from that cycle.
 This check supplies a configured delay margin; it does not measure pose age, prove
 physical stopping dynamics, or certify delays beyond the chosen hold time.
 Continuous-60 simulation success remains a separate validation requirement.
+
+### Curvature-limited RPP (Humble)
+
+`cleany_navigation::CurvatureLimitedRPP` delegates to native Nav2 RPP and
+proportionally reduces returned `linear.x` and `angular.z` when the yaw exceeds
+`FollowPath.tracking_yaw_limit` (default 0.14 rad/s, finite and positive).
+Unlike independently clipping yaw, this retains the returned turning radius.
+The native footprint and forward collision checks still run before scaling;
+exceptions propagate. This is a command-path invariant, not a continuous
+collision or tracking guarantee under actuator dynamics and downstream guards.
+
+Set this controller as `FollowPath.plugin`, or as `FollowPath.wrapped_plugin`
+when using the benchmark TimedController. The yaw limit is configure-time only;
+attempts to change it while configured are rejected. Cleanup/reconfigure to
+change it. Other native RPP parameters retain their upstream behavior.
+No native linear acceleration limit or shared smoother is added. Preserve the
+platform's final guard, footprint, tolerance and wheel constraints.
+
+Humble's terminal rotation predicate compares the carrot distance with goal
+XY tolerance. A minimum lookahead smaller than that tolerance can therefore
+trigger goal rotation away from the goal; keep the floor above the tolerance
+when using velocity-scaled lookahead. With a fixed-heading holonomic global
+path, this forward-only controller still follows the path tangent and may be
+unable to rotate its padded footprint at a narrow endpoint.
+
+RPP Gazebo tuning and one-pass common-goal evidence are retained under
+`controller-optimization-20261013/rpp/sol61_20261013_0620/` outside this checkout.
diff --git a/ros2_ws/src/cleany_navigation/include/cleany_navigation/rpp_yaw_limit.hpp b/ros2_ws/src/cleany_navigation/include/cleany_navigation/rpp_yaw_limit.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..80f60b1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ros2_ws/src/cleany_navigation/include/cleany_navigation/rpp_yaw_limit.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+#ifndef CLEANY_NAVIGATION__RPP_YAW_LIMIT_HPP_
+#define CLEANY_NAVIGATION__RPP_YAW_LIMIT_HPP_
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <stdexcept>
+namespace cleany_navigation
+{
+inline double rpp_yaw_scale(double angular, double limit)
+{
+  if (!std::isfinite(limit) || limit <= 0.0) {
+    throw std::invalid_argument("tracking_yaw_limit must be finite and positive");
+  }
+  if (!std::isfinite(angular)) {
+    throw std::invalid_argument("native RPP returned a non-finite angular velocity");
+  }
+  return std::abs(angular) > limit ? limit / std::abs(angular) : 1.0;
+}
+}  // namespace cleany_navigation
+#endif  // CLEANY_NAVIGATION__RPP_YAW_LIMIT_HPP_
